From 7ca5d3885b38773adb2b13b3dab5bdae0c4a0d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:53:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/67] Keep entry count in sync when splitting zero-page loads

JoinEntryLoadStoreZP moves a zero-page load/store pair at the top of a
block into the predecessors that can take it, and sends the others
through a new block that holds the pair. It removed each of those
predecessors from the block's entry list without decrementing
mNumEntries, then added the new block as an entry and incremented it, so
the count exceeded mEntryBlocks.Size() by the number of predecessors
moved. RemoveUnusedResultInstructions then fails its assertion
"mIndex == 1000 || mNumEntries == mEntryBlocks.Size()".

Decrement the count for each predecessor removed, as
PartialBackwardValuePropagation does when it moves entries to a new
block. The increment when the new block joins remains correct.

It is nethack64's repro r60: NetHack's mattackm() (mhitm.c) aborted
native code generation once the measurement harness kept its stub
functions out of line.

Written by Codex; checked by Claude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
index cde8668..1a95b10 100644
--- a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -30701,6 +30701,7 @@ bool NativeCodeBasicBlock::JoinEntryLoadStoreZP(void)
 									if (eb->mFalseJump == this)
 										eb->mFalseJump = xblock;
 									mEntryBlocks.Remove(j);
+									mNumEntries--;
 									xblock->mEntryBlocks.Push(eb);
 									xblock->mNumEntries++;
 								}
